<title>USA: US aluminum center shipments dip 2 pct Jan to Nov.</title>
<headline>US aluminum center shipments dip 2 pct Jan to Nov.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Service center shipments of aluminum mill products in the United States for the eleven months ended November 1996 were two percent below shipments for the same period in 1995, the National Association of Aluminum Distributors said.</p>
<p>According to NAAD's three month moving average index, shipments in November fell to 138.8 points from 139.7 points in October. Inventory rose to 119.8 points from 119.3 over the same period.</p>
<p>Service center inventories in November remained at 2.7 months, a level maintained since September.</p>
<p>((New York Commodities 212-859-1646))</p>
</text>
